BullMQ Lua scripts (expanded)
================================

Files in this directory:

  cleanJobsInSet.lua   cleanJobsInSet:3
  getCounts.lua        getCounts:1
  getRanges.lua        getRanges:1
  pause.lua            pause:7
  promote.lua          promote:9
  removeJob.lua        removeJob:2
  reprocessJob.lua     reprocessJob:8

Origin
------

Extracted from the locked dependency in this repository:

  node_modules/.pnpm/bullmq@5.63.2/node_modules/bullmq/dist/cjs/scripts/*.js

Each file there embeds the fully expanded script (the `--- @include` directives
of `dist/cjs/commands/*.lua` resolved and de-duplicated at build time) as the
`content` template literal. The files here are that embedded content copied
verbatim, so the include expansion and the function ordering are exactly what
BullMQ 5.63.2 executes against Redis.

The expansion was checked against `dist/cjs/commands/` for every file: the
`content` literal matches a recursive `--- @include` expansion of
`commands/<name>.lua`, except that the build inlines each include once. A naive
recursive expansion therefore duplicates include fragments and must not be used.

The four scripts that bullmqcleanup already vendors (cleanJobsInSet, getCounts,
getRanges, removeJob) are byte-identical to
`apps/api-go/internal/bullmqcleanup/scripts/*.lua`; the copies here exist so this
package is self-contained and can be reviewed against the call sites in one
directory.

Why the scripts are vendored
----------------------------

The queue operations console calls the same Redis entry points Bull Board calls
through BullMQ: Queue.getJobCounts, Queue.getJobs, Queue.clean, Queue.pause,
Queue.resume, Job.retry, Job.promote and Job.remove. Each of those resolves to
one of the scripts above. Re-implementing the lock, marker, deduplication and
event semantics in Go would drift from BullMQ; running the same Lua keeps the
observable queue state identical to the NestJS process that still runs the
workers.

The Go call sites pass the same KEYS/ARGV tuples the matching BullMQ JavaScript
methods build in `classes/scripts.js` of the same version:

  getCounts        keys [prefix]                                    args [state...]
  getRanges        keys [prefix]                     args [start, end, asc, state...]
  removeJob        keys [jobKey, repeatKey]           args [jobId, removeChildren, prefix]
  cleanJobsInSet   keys [setKey, events, repeat]      args [prefix, timestamp, limit, set]
  reprocessJob     keys [jobKey, events, stateKey,
                          wait, meta, paused, active,
                          marker]                       args [jobId, pushCmd, propVal, state]
  promote          keys [delayed, wait, paused, meta,
                          prioritized, active, pc,
                          events, marker]               args [prefix, jobId]
  pause            keys [srcList, dstList, meta,
                          prioritized, events,
                          delayed, marker]              args ['paused' | 'resumed']

`pause:7` is shared by Queue.pause and Queue.resume: pause passes
KEYS[1]=wait, KEYS[2]=paused and ARGV[1]='paused'; resume swaps the two lists and
passes 'resumed'.

